  "answer": "I'll start by looking at the workspace and the relevant files.\nThe bug is clear: the loop subtracts instead of adds. Let me fix it.\nFixed and verified.\n\n## The bug\n\n`src/ledger.ts` accumulated totals with subtraction:\n\n```ts\nsum -= entry.amount   // wrong: each entry reduced the total\n```\n\n## The fix\n\nSingle-line change — the accumulator now adds every entry, as the running total semantics require:\n\n```ts\nsum += entry.amount\n```\n\n## What stayed untouched\n\n- Exported shape unchanged: `Entry { amount: number }` and `total(entries: Entry[]): number`.\n- `package.json`, `AGENTS.md`, and `test/oracle.test.ts` are unmodified; no config added and the runner is still `bun test`.\n\n## Test run\n\n```\nbun test v1.3.14\ntest/oracle.test.ts:\n(pass) totals add [0.14ms]\n 1 pass, 0 fail, 3 expect() calls\n```\n\nAll three assertions hold: `[4, 6] → 10`, `[] → 0`, and `[{ amount: -3 }] → -3`. Note that negative entries still yield a negative contribution — that falls out of addition itself, so no subtraction is needed anywhere, and the function no longer inverts signs on any input."
